  "issue_number": 20,
  "issue_title": "fix(validator): fail closed webhook auth when secret is unset/default (#18)",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nCloses #18\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes a security bug where webhook authentication could be silently bypassed when `GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET` was unset or left at the default `replace-me`.\r\n\r\nIn `validator/src/eval_backend/api/routes.py`, webhook validators previously returned early for missing/default secrets, which allowed unauthenticated webhook traffic in misconfigured deployments.\r\n\r\n## What Changed\r\n- Added `_ensure_webhook_secret_configured(...)` to enforce secret configuration.\r\n- Updated `_verify_github_signature(...)` to:\r\n  - fail with `500` when webhook secret is unset/default\r\n  - continue returning `401` for missing/invalid GitHub signatures\r\n- Updated `_verify_shared_secret(...)` to:\r\n  - fail with `500` when webhook secret is unset/default\r\n  - continue returning `401` for missing/invalid shared secret values\r\n- Added unit tests in `validator/tests/test_webhook_auth.py` for:\r\n  - fail-closed default/missing secret behavior\r\n  - invalid signature/secret rejection\r\n  - valid signature/secret acceptance\r\n\r\n## Why This Matters\r\nThis makes webhook auth fail-closed by default and prevents accidental insecure deployments from accepting forged webhook requests.\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\nA corresponding replication log entry was added to `docs/JOURNAL.md` per repository protocol.",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-12T02:12:04.000Z",
  "test_cmd": [
    "python",
    "-m",
    "pytest",
    "--tb=short",
    "-q",
    "validator/tests/test_webhook_auth.py"
  ],
